{"id":102678582775882,"type":"album","name":"Apostrophe (')","artist":"Frank Zappa","year":1974,"weight":13,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/28251-apostrophe-.jpg","aoty":77,"aoty_user":83,"yt":"mpNn1nht0_8","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/frank-zappa/apostrophe-","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/28251-frank-zappa-apostrophe-.php"},"desc":"Apostrophe (') is the fifth solo album and eighteenth in total by Frank Zappa, released in March 1974 in both stereo and quadraphonic formats. An edited version of its lead-off track, \"Don't Eat the Yellow Snow\", was the first of Zappa's three Billboard Top 100 hits, ultimately peaking at number 86. The album itself became the biggest commercial success of Zappa's career, reaching number 10 on the US Billboard 200. Apostrophe (') remains Zappa's most commercially successful album in the United States. It was certified gold by the RIAA on April 7, 1976 and peaked at number 10 (a career-high ."},"artist_ref":{"id":48325419023266,"name":"Frank Zappa","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Zappa.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":138197775829889,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":439,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":117363531556446,"type":"genre","name":"Jazz-Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":263,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":133646791193319,"type":"genre","name":"Laurel Canyon Scene","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":145636818792428,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jazz-Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":11,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":177455037556203,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Laurel Canyon Scene","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"